  "worked_solution": "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-10$ the function has a corner, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=-5$ the function has an infinite discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-10$ and $x=-5.$",
